{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504423,"nonce":"YUDCQp6TJHk5F9Bw8uJmBMSiOTU=","title":"`ingest_rejections` has an index built for a rejection feed and no read path anywhere that uses it","was":"**What is wrong.** Every per-alert bound failure and every terminal batch failure is durably recorded, and nothing in the product can read it back. `internal/ingestion/repository/rejections.go` declares exactly two methods, `Record` and `RecordBatch` — both writes. `internal/ingestion/repository/batches.go` declares `Insert`, `Get`, `MarkProcessed` and `ResolveOrg`, and `Get` requires the caller to already know both `batch_id` and `received_at`, which only the job handler does. Of the 85 `operationId`s in `api/openapi/openapi.yaml`, none reads a rejection or lists a batch. Nothing in `web/src` consumes either table. The operator whose alert never appeared has `psql` as the only diagnostic."}]}